This one I don't like... the main problem with the current bard patch
is exactly the overwhelming number of songs; it looks like an entire
spellcasting system of its own. I prefer to go for the idea of few
songs having different effects; adding more subtleties to the music
system to make it different of the spellcasting system. Sure, there
will be more than three songs, but dozens of them is too much.
I want to try something simple. I think I'll make the bard play only
three general melodies with basic skill in music: Peaceful melody,
Scary melody, and Battle cry. A peaceful melody, for example, can make
a monster become peaceful or sleep, randomly. As the bard increases
his music skills he can play more 'refined' versions of these
melodies: Peace, Sleep, etc. which have better success rates and are
targeted to specific effects.

Being helped by music playing pets is an interesting idea... but the
only ones I can think of are satyrs and nymphs. Maybe they could
increase the success rate?

The quest artifact is the Lyre of Harmony, which belonged to Orpheus,
your quest leader. The idea is that it can play any kind of music with
better success rates (thus relieving you of having to carry lots of
instruments). But I think it can still get a penalty for playing
offensive/scary music, and having some advantage in playing peaceful
music, since the instrument purpose is create harmony. Not sure about
the #invoke effect, though. By "E-word song" you mean being
invulnerable while the song is played?

